# Topics Server Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values
#
# WARNING: Topics has no built-in authentication.
# Do not expose it to the public internet without additional security.

# Server settings
PORT=3333

# ==== AI provider ====
# Leave AI_PROVIDER UNSET. What "unset" actually does, in the order the code
# does it (server.ts, then server/providers/index.ts recomputeDefault):
#
#   1. The BOOT default comes from your keys, not from a ranking:
#      ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -> claude, else OPENAI_API_KEY -> openai, else
#      claude with no key at all.
#   2. That default is KEPT for as long as it reports connected. The ranking
#      below never runs while it is up.
#   3. Only when the current default goes offline is a replacement chosen, and
#      only then by PROVIDER_PREFERENCE_ORDER (server/providers/index.ts) —
#      its own docstring calls it the order "di RIPIEGO", the fallback one:
#
#        claude-code -> codex -> muse -> claude -> openai
#
#      It is subscription-first (the local CLIs your Claude/ChatGPT/Muse login
#      already pays for rank above the metered API keys), it ranks only
#      CONNECTED providers, and a provider outside the table falls below all
#      five rather than being skipped.
#
# So: set an API key and you have chosen that key's provider as the default.
# If you want the CLI your subscription pays for, do not set the key — or pin
# it below.
#
# Being registered is not the same as being there. Two providers appear in the
# picker without their backend: `claude` is always registered at boot (with an
# empty key, as the last-resort default so the picker has a target), and
# `claude-code` is registered by CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLED even with no CLI on PATH.
# The rest are registered only when they are really there: the codex or muse
# CLI on PATH, OPENAI_API_KEY.
#
# Setting it here pins one provider and beats connectivity: the pin wins even
# when that provider is offline, and a chat aimed at a CLI you never installed
# errors. This file used to ship a pinned AI_PROVIDER, and README says to copy
# it to .env, so every fresh clone inherited exactly that.
#
# Valid values: claude-code | codex | muse | claude | openai
# ACP agents (gemini and friends) are NOT valid here. They are registered
# automatically and chosen per topic.
# AI_PROVIDER=claude-code

# For Claude provider (Anthropic API)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-20250514

# App data directory: media, workspace, sessions. Defaults to the legacy
# folder in your home when it already exists, else ~/.topics
# (server/lib/data-dir.ts).
# APP_DATA_DIR=/path/to/data

# Sessions directory (defaults to $APP_DATA_DIR/agents/main/sessions)
# SESSIONS_DIR=/path/to/sessions

# ElevenLabs (optional) - text-to-speech AND Scribe v2 speech-to-text
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=your-elevenlabs-api-key-here

# ==== Dictation / speech-to-text ====
# With no config at all, /api/stt tries, in order, whichever it can:
#   ElevenLabs scribe_v2 -> OpenAI gpt-transcribe -> Deepgram nova-3
#   -> Groq whisper-large-v3-turbo -> local whisper.cpp (ffmpeg + whisper-cli)
# A provider is "available" when its key is set; the first that answers wins.
# STT_PROVIDER=auto           # or: openai | elevenlabs | deepgram | groq | local | "openai,local"
# STT_LANGUAGE=auto           # ISO-639-1 (it, en, ...) — auto-detect when unset
# STT_MODEL_OPENAI=gpt-transcribe
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# Local whisper.cpp only: model auto-discovered under ~/whisper-models etc.
# WHISPER_MODEL_PATH=/path/to/ggml-large-v3-turbo.bin

# ==== Phase 30 BROWSER-CHAT-03 -- Moondream vision fallback (optional) ====
# The browser_point tool uses this for canvas/captcha grounding.
# Get key from: https://moondream.ai (Cloud Account -> API keys)
# If unset, browser_point returns a structured error -- the other 5 browser_*
# tools (open/observe/act/extract/screenshot) work without it.
# MOONDREAM_API_KEY=md_xxx...

# Per-context budget for browser_point calls (default 5). Counter is reset
# when the BrowserContext is destroyed (e.g. topic browser closed).
# MOONDREAM_MAX_CALLS_PER_TASK=5

# ==== Discord Rich Presence (optional) ====
# The Application ID that appears as the card name in Discord.
# The default ships as the official "Topics" application on the Discord
# Developer Portal (discord.com/developers/applications).
# Override only if you registered your own application and want YOUR name
# shown instead of "Topics".
# DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=your-application-id-here
